      "The Gospels describe John as the son of Zechariah, a priest, and Elizabeth, who was related to Mary. Luke says that the angel Gabriel announced John's birth to Zechariah while he was serving in the Temple. The child was given the name John, despite the family's expectation that he would be named after his father. Luke presents his birth as a sign that God was preparing a prophet who would call Israel back to faithful living.",
      "John grew up and began preaching in the wilderness of Judea, calling people to repentance because the Kingdom of God was near. He baptised those who confessed their sins in the Jordan River, and his ministry drew crowds from Jerusalem and the surrounding region. His austere clothing and simple way of life recalled the prophet Elijah. John made clear that he was not the Messiah: he was preparing the way for someone greater who would baptise with the Holy Spirit.",
