      "Concerned that the Carmelite life had become less demanding than its original ideal, Teresa began a reform that sought greater simplicity, prayer and community discipline. In 1562 she founded the convent of St. Joseph in Ávila, the first house of the reformed or Discalced Carmelite nuns. Despite opposition, she travelled across Spain and established further communities. She worked closely with John of the Cross, who helped lead a parallel reform among Carmelite friars.",
